# 2. IMPORTANT DEVELOPMENT SCOPE

This project is FRONTEND ONLY.

Do not create or implement:
- Node.js backend.
- Express server.
- SQLite database.
- Database schema.
- Backend authentication logic.
- Backend API routes.
- Database migrations.
- Server-side notification jobs.
- Backend business logic.

However, structure the frontend so that it can connect to the backend later without redesigning the application.

Use:
- React API service files.
- Centralized API configuration.
- Reusable data-fetching hooks.
- Authentication context.
- Protected route components.
- Structured request and response handling.
- Mock data adapters only when the actual backend is unavailable.

IMPORTANT:

Do not mix mock data directly into React page components.

Keep mock services separate from real API services so they can be replaced later.

All buttons, links, tabs, filters, forms and interactions must perform their expected frontend actions.

Do not create decorative buttons that do nothing.

If an action requires a backend that is not connected yet, provide a clearly separated mock implementation and document that it must be replaced when the backend becomes available.

