## Admin Route

Accessible only when the authenticated user has ADMIN role.

Examples:
- Admin Dashboard.
- Cycle Management.
- Booking Management.
- Sales.
- Payments.
- Reports.
- Settings.

After login:
- Customer goes to customer area.
- Admin goes to admin dashboard.

If a customer attempts to open an admin page:
- Do not render admin content.
- Show unauthorized or redirect to an appropriate page.

If an admin opens a customer-only page, handle it according to the route policy.

When the session expires:
- Clear frontend authentication state.
- Redirect to the appropriate login page.
- Show a session-expired message.

IMPORTANT:

Frontend route protection is a user-interface feature, not the security boundary.

The backend must independently verify every protected operation when connected.

Never trust a role value supplied or modified by the browser.

